(Northstar Operations Group - PTO Policy) Tj
T*
T*
(# PTO Policy) Tj
T*
T*
(1. Eligibility) Tj
T*
(Full-time employees are eligible for paid time off after their start date.) Tj
T*
(Part-time employees receive PTO only when their offer letter or local law) Tj
T*
(requires it.) Tj
T*
T*
(2. Annual PTO Amount) Tj
T*
(Full-time employees receive 20 PTO days per calendar year, equal to 160 hours.) Tj
T*
(New hires receive a prorated amount based on start date. PTO balances are shown) Tj
T*
(in the HR system of record.) Tj
T*
T*
(3. Request Process) Tj
T*
(Employees should submit PTO requests in the HR system at least 10 business days) Tj
T*
(before planned time away when practical. The employee's manager reviews the) Tj
T*
(request for team coverage, deadlines, and business impact.) Tj
T*
T*
(4. Approval Authority) Tj
T*
(Only the employee's manager or a designated HR approver may approve PTO. The) Tj
T*
(knowledge assistant, coworkers, and informal chat messages cannot approve PTO or) Tj
T*
(override the HR system.) Tj
T*
T*
(5. Escalation) Tj
T*
(Employees with questions about balances, leave laws, medical leave, or) Tj
T*
(accommodation-related time away should contact HR. Managers should consult HR) Tj
T*
(before denying complex leave requests.) Tj
